{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>And he put him into the house of the round prison, the place where the king's prisoners were confined</b>. Rabbi Abraham said that Scripture explains that 'the house of the sohar' is the place where the king's prisoners are confined there, and therefore he said that it is an Egyptian term, for it is the way of Scripture to explain a foreign expression, as in 'he cast pur, that is, the lot' (Esther 3:7). But he said nothing at all; rather, 'and he put him into the house of the sohar' — the one known to the king, which is the place where the king's prisoners would be confined — is to say that this was the reason the cupbearer and the baker entered with him. And it is possible that the reason for 'the king's prisoners' is his servants and ministers who sin against him under royal jurisdiction, for other prisoners belonging to the people are in the hands of the judges and officers and would be placed in a different prison. And Scripture relates that they placed Joseph there because of his master's love for him, and all of it was a cause from HaShem. And the masters of the language (Radak in Sefer HaShorashim, root סהר) explained 'sahar' as a round basin, from the expression 'agan hasahar' (Song of Songs 7:3). And in my opinion it is the bor (Ramban on Genesis 40:2): a house built underground with a small opening above through which they bring the prisoners in, and from it light comes to them. And it is from the Aramaic סֵיהֲרָא, as Scripture said (Genesis 6:16), 'a tzohar you shall make for the ark,' from the word צָהֳרַיִם (noon), and they interchanged in it — this one for abundance of light and that one for paucity."], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 39, :notes {0 "The parenthetical reference to Radak and the cross-reference to Ramban on Genesis 40:2 appear to be editorial annotations inserted into the text; they are translated as they appear in the source."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:42:12.876816373Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}